# CLAUDE.local.md (personal overrides — gitignored)

> Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` and fill in your personal settings. This file is gitignored and overrides defaults in `CLAUDE.md`. Claude Code reads both files automatically; values here take precedence.

## Research Domain

Describe your research focus in one sentence. This replaces the generic header in `CLAUDE.md`.

Example:
> A personal knowledge base of {your-field} papers focused on {topic-1}, {topic-2}, and {topic-3}.

## Categories

Replace the placeholder categories in `CLAUDE.md` with your actual research areas.

| Category | Includes |
|---|---|
| `your-topic-1` | (specific scope) |
| `your-topic-2` | (specific scope) |
| `your-topic-3` | (specific scope) |
| `methods` | Methods and tools papers |
| `concepts` | Theory and methodology |
| `overviews` | Synthesis pages |
| `other` | Cross-cutting |

Create matching subfolders under `wiki/{category}/`.

## Tool Paths (Optional)

If you use Mendeley:

```yaml
mendeley_userfiles_path: /path/to/your/Mendeley/userfiles
```

If you use a local LLM, point to its endpoint:

```yaml
local_llm_endpoint: http://localhost:1234/v1
local_llm_model: your-model-name
```

## Personal Identifiers

- email: your@email.com
- preferred citation style: (e.g., APA, Nature, Cell)
- timezone: (e.g., America/Los_Angeles)
